---
// Topics listed in the margin so readers can scan them at a glance.
const topics = [
  'Software engineering',
  'AI for software engineering',
  'Programming systems',
  'Program analysis',
];
const alsoOpen = ['Databases', 'Distributed systems'];
---

<div class="row">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      My research interests lie in software engineering, AI for software engineering, and programming systems and
      program analysis, especially at the intersections of these areas. I am also open to exploring related areas such
      as databases and distributed systems. I am particularly interested in how we can design and build software
      systems that are reliable, scalable, and less error-prone, and in how agentic AI pipelines can be used in
      practice across every stage of the software development lifecycle (development, debugging, testing, and
      deployment), not just for code generation.
    </p>
  </div>
  <aside class="note topics">
    <ul>{topics.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}</ul>
    <p><em>Also:</em> {alsoOpen.join(', ').toLowerCase()}</p>
  </aside>
</div>

<style>
  .topics li::before { content: '– '; }
  .topics p { margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  @media (max-width: 879px) {
    .topics { display: none; }
  }
</style>
